# UX Screens & States — VTC Apps

Visual styling: `ui.mdc` (App Shell, **Typography Standard**). Business list behavior: `business-patterns.mdc`. Landing: `landing-page.mdc`.

## Screen Philosophy

- Apps should be **functional first** — user opens the app to do a task, not read a summary.
- **Do not add a dashboard** unless the brief clearly needs KPIs/summary or the user asks.
- Default authenticated entry: **primary list** or **primary task screen** (e.g. today’s bookings, invoice list).
- **Use the standard App Shell** on every authenticated screen — sticky header with **header action slots**, responsive container (`ui.mdc`), standard nav. Do not invent custom navigation patterns (sidebars, bottom tabs, bottom action bars, hamburger menus, FABs).
- **Desktop lists must not use 450px width** — default `max-w-[900px]` unless the screen is form-focused.

## Page Templates (App Shell)

| Page type | Container | Layout | Reference |
|-----------|-----------|--------|-----------|
| **List / task home** | `max-w-[900px]` | App Shell header + search/filters + list | Below |
| **Admin / create / edit** | `450px` short forms · `900px` standard editors | Header slots + form + collapsible panels | `ui.mdc` |
| **Public content / detail** | `max-w-[760px]` | Top actions + hero + title/metadata + body | `ui.mdc` |
| **Visual / grid browse** | `max-w-[1100px]`–`1200px` | Toolbar + grid/masonry | `ui.mdc` |
| **Promotional landing** | — | No App Shell — marketing layout | `landing-page.mdc` |

### Articles app

| Screen | Container |
|--------|-----------|
| Article list | `max-w-[900px]` |
| Article detail | `max-w-[760px]` |
| Article editor | `max-w-[900px]` |

**Admin entry:** ellipsis menu item by default — never plain text links or text menus in the top bar (`ui.mdc`).

## Minimum Screen Set (CRUD entity)

| Screen | Route (example) | Required |
|--------|-----------------|----------|
| Promotional landing | `/` | Yes — `landing-page.mdc` |
| List | `/items` or `/` when list is home | Yes |
| Create | `/items/new` or modal | Yes |
| Edit | `/items/[id]/edit` or modal | Yes |
| Detail | `/items/[id]` | Optional — use when read-only view helps |

**Dashboard** — omit unless user or brief requires it.

## Required UI States (Every Data Screen)

Implement all four — do not ship a blank screen while loading or on failure.

| State | When | Pattern |
|-------|------|---------|
| **Loading** | Initial fetch / submit | Skeleton or spinner; button `disabled` + loading label |
| **Empty** | Success, zero records | Illustration/message + primary CTA (e.g. “Create first item”) |
| **Error** | `success: false` or network fail | Inline banner or message; retry action |
| **No results** | Search/filter returned 0 | Distinct from empty — “No matches for …” + clear filters |

## List Screen

- Container: **`max-w-[900px]`** (standard CRUD default) — not `450px`
- **Search** input (debounced fetch with `q`)
- **Filters** when status or category matters (tabs or dropdown → API params)
- App Shell sticky header — **embedded (default):** no app name (platform chrome shows it); **standalone:** app title in bar. Embedded home has **no app-name heading or subtitle** (no "Your personal X") — first element is content or a primary action (`ui.mdc` § Platform shell chrome). Header action slots — `ui.mdc` **Header action slots**
- Page title in `<main>`: `text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white` — not in top bar
- Create via **header slot 1** (`Plus`); search/filter via **slot 2** — `ui.mdc` **Header action slots**

## Create / Edit

- **Admin/edit layout** — `ui.mdc`: header slots (slot 1 = Save) + form + collapsible panels — no bottom bar
- Same form component where possible; mode from route or prop
- Floating-label inputs (`ui.mdc`)
- Cancel via `BackButton`; no `confirm()`

## Detail / Public Content

- Container: **`max-w-[760px]`** (reading tier)
- **Public content layout** — `ui.mdc`: top action row, optional hero, title/metadata, body
- Use when read-only view or article-like content helps; optional route `/items/[id]`

## Navigation

- Preserve `token`, `mode`, `lang` via `addTokenToUrl()` (`auth-bootstrap.mdc`)
- `BackButton` on nested screens only — not on list home
- No custom nav chrome — stay within App Shell patterns

## i18n

No hardcoded user-visible strings — keys in `src/locales/en.json` (+ `es`, `pt` stubs when scaffolding). See `i18n.mdc`.
